# Files that run on the server must keep LF endings regardless of who checks
# them out. A shell script that arrives with CRLF fails on Linux with the
# famously unhelpful `bash: \r: command not found`, and nginx/systemd units are
# equally unforgiving.
*.sh            text eol=lf
*.mjs           text eol=lf
*.conf          text eol=lf
Dockerfile      text eol=lf
Caddyfile       text eol=lf
.env.example    text eol=lf
*.service       text eol=lf
*.timer         text eol=lf
